Add ${JPEG_PKG} to the deps target list

OrcaSlicer sets JPEG_PKG=dep_JPEG when JPEG isn't already found on the
system (deps/CMakeLists.txt:~420), but never actually adds it to the
_dep_list top-level target. On desktop builds, OpenCV's internal
libjpeg (BUILD_JPEG=ON) covered the need via OpenCV's bundled libs.

On Android, OpenCV is built with -DWITH_JPEG=OFF (per its recipe), so
no libjpeg is produced anywhere — and libslic3r's
    find_package(JPEG REQUIRED)   # src/libslic3r/CMakeLists.txt:544
fails. Add ${JPEG_PKG} to _dep_list so the existing JPEG.cmake recipe
actually runs.

Retire-if: upstream adds JPEG to _dep_list, or switches libslic3r away
from find_package(JPEG).

---
diff --git a/deps/CMakeLists.txt b/deps/CMakeLists.txt
index d592dac959..202605ce44 100644
--- a/deps/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/deps/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -473,6 +473,7 @@ set(_dep_list
     ${GLFW_PKG}
     dep_OCCT
     ${FREETYPE_PKG}
+    ${JPEG_PKG}
     ${PNG_PKG}
     ${ZLIB_PKG}
     ${EXPAT_PKG}
